<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02TE">Remark <span data-tag="02TE">7.4.4.10</span>.</a> In the situation of Construction <a data-tag="02TD" href="/tag/02TD">7.4.4.9</a>, let $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a vertex and let $\operatorname{ev}_{C}: \operatorname{Fun}_{/ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\operatorname{CCart}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$ be the evaluation functor, given on objects by $\operatorname{ev}_{C}(F) = F(C)$. Then the composition </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}_{ {\bf 0} } \xrightarrow {\mathrm{Df}} \operatorname{Fun}_{/ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\operatorname{CCart}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \xrightarrow {\operatorname{ev}_ C} \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C} \]
</div>
<p> is given by covariant transport along the unique edge ${\bf 0} \rightarrow C$ of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\triangleleft }$. </p>
</article>
